> Interpretation and limits

Distinct finite sites are required; duplicate sites throw instead of
double-counting a cell. Sites may lie outside the viewport and have empty cells.
Long-double bisector arithmetic improves conditioning but is not an
exact-predicate geometry guarantee. The original24 seeded sites are retained,
while the figure now uses true cells clipped to[0,10]² at equal Cartesian
scales.

All programs are complete editable C++ sources; figures are local files. Actual
traces and selected counts come from the producing native kernels, not an
independent report reconstruction.

> References

Squared-distance cancellation and convex half-plane intersection are derived
above; the legacy dual API and new clipped API have distinct stated contracts.

